{"text": "PROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE\nVirginia Department of Rail and Public Transportation \u2014 Richmond, VA July 2006 to Present\n\nDRPT is the state agency for rail and public transportation in Virginia, operating through three business areas of\nrail, transit and transportation demand management. DRPT\u2019s has an annual budget of over $624 million that\nleverages an overall program of $1.55 billion in rail and transit initiatives. DRPT supports more than 50 public\ntransit agencies, 50 human service transportation providers, 15 transportation demand management agencies, and\ncollaborates with 12 privately owned railroad companies.\n\nAppointed as the Agency Director by Governor Timothy M. Kaine in June 2006. Reports directly to the Secretary\nof Transportation and is responsive to two boards, the Commonwealth Transportation Board and the Rail Advisory\nBoard. Introduced significant new measures to strengthen DRPT\u2019s organization and operations through the\ndevelopment of improved performance indicators. Increased accountability for the investment of public funds and\ndeveloped new management principles for agency programs.\n\nAGENCY DIRECTOR\n\nResponsible for directing the operations of DRPT, the state agency for rail and transit in Virginia, including six\nfunctional units that include strategic planning, rail/transit special projects, transit and transportation demand\nmanagement, rail transportation and state safety oversight, finance and administration, and policy and\ncommunication.\n\n\u201cWorks closely with federal, state, and local elected officials regarding transportation programs and projects.\n\u201c Leads the development of statewide plans for rail, public transportation, and transportation demand\nmanagement.\n~ Implemented an agency reorganization to enhance agency performance across business areas, increase\naccountability and increase efficiency.\n\u201c+ Executed numerous agreements with public entities and private freight railroad companies to reduce\ncongestion.\n\u201c Managed the transition of a $5 billion transit project to extend heavy rail service in the Dulles Corridor to the\nMetropolitan Washington Area Airports Authority.\n\u201c Coordinates with the Virginia Department of Transportation for the planning of significant highway projects.\n\nSanta Clara Valley Transportation Authority - San Jose, California April 2001 to July 2006\n\nVTA is responsible for bus and light rail operations, regional commuter and inter-city rail service, ADA paratransit,\ncongestion management, specific highway improvement projects, and countywide transportation planning in Santa\nClara County. The Transit Operations Division had more than 1,700 employees and an operating budget of $264\nmillion in FY 06. Transit ridership across all modes and services totaled more than 40 million annually.\nCHIEF OPERATING OFFICER\n\nResponsible for directing VTA transit operations, comprising six functional units that included bus operations, rail\noperations, protective services, service and operations planning, support services and engineering. Prior to being\npromoted to Chief Operating Officer, served as Director of Transportation and Maintenance and Deputy Director\n\nfor Bus and Rail Transportation.\nMATTHEW O. TUCKER",
